mantle rm264
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rmx_dorcas_brineley
title the thumb on the high note
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=laborer
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=devout drive=restless
quirk mutes_the_high_note_with_a_thumb_to_the_throat
likes blackberries singing old_maps frosty_mornings
dislikes gulls haggling
fears a_public_cry_turning_to_a_jeer
hopes a_song_with_nobody_being_sold_anything
topics work +0.6 faith +0.5 pastimes +0.4 gossip -0.5
styles comfort=steadfast gossip=guarded refuse=plain tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# sets a thumb to the throat for the pitch of a cry and saves a private note for the Bright One.

words
oath! = Pinch my last note | Turn my tune inside out
saying! = A mouth can sell the cloth and keep the tune | High notes won't mend a torn cuff
call = a long clear cry | a two-note call
berrymark = a purple thumbprint | a spot of berry stain
mapfold = an old worn fold | a tucked paper corner
hemband = a strip of selvedge | a narrow hem
restgap = a space for breath | a pause between cries
hoodtip = the folded tip | the hood's edge
firstbar = the low opening note | the first two beats
lastbar = a note going up | a slow falling note
roofslope = the slope above market | the highest slates
coldair = a breath of white air | a clear cold breath
wingnoise = a racket of wings | the churning above the stalls
handmark = a sign made with one paw | a sweep of the wrist

any
opinion houses against 3 : Some loads come home in full and some leave a space at supper. I remember who counts them.
opinion church for 2 : A market voice can find a quiet use before the Bright One.
opinion merchants mixed 1 : I can admire a good piece of cloth without thinking the wolf who wove it got a fair share.
opinion festivals for 1 : It's a relief singing to a street where nobody expects a list of sizes.
opinion sump for 2 : Every low roof has a different answer to my call. I'd miss that chorus.
opinion dole for 2 : A wolf can be too hungry to shout and still have a perfectly good claim on supper.

grown
line greet : Ease your ears. This greeting's just for you. | I'm off my high note. Welcome.
line greet.return : A private greeting coming right back. | Glad our voices met at this softer pitch.
line again.open : Back before the echo quite died.
line farewell : Go with a clear throat and an easy stride. | I'll save the next cry till you're clear.
line farewell.return : And a fair wind behind your words. | My good wishes don't need shouting after you.
line react.news : Speak close. I'd sooner hear than carry it. | Let that news use your own voice.
line react.news.new : That's a tune freshly come to this street.
line react.news.known : The second hearing carries just as far.
line react.news.doubt : Somebody's reached above the comfortable notes.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|assault] : I'd lay my market voice aside for news so sore.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work] : That deserves all the lift my voice can give it.
line ask.how : Has your own voice carried far today?
line answer.how : A bit rubbed at the edges. I can still hum.
line sympathise : You can whisper it if that's easier.
line reassure : Nobody need find the high note straight away.
line refuse : My voice is promised elsewhere before the light goes.
line accept_decline : You needn't shout a refusal twice.
line preclose : I have another bit of street to cover yet.
line accept_preclose : I'll let you go without a final flourish.
line ack : Yes, quite clear through the bustle.

scene exchange1
when topic=work self.job=laborer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I start my market cry below speaking pitch. | I give the colour first and the cloth after.
b : Can anybody hear that? | Does it sell better that way?
a : The second note rises clean out of it. | A red sleeve gets a look before linen gets an ear.

scene exchange2
when topic=faith self.piety=devout
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I take my thumb off my throat to pray. | I pray after the busiest part of market.
b : Why put it there otherwise? | Why wait?
a : I measure my selling voice. A prayer can go as it is. | I can offer the Bright One my listening then too.

scene exchange3
when topic=animals self.dislikes=gulls
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A gull cuts in just above my highest note. | I won't compete with gulls for air.
b : Do the buyers take any notice? | Do you close the stall?
a : Some look up. A gull hasn't sold one sleeve yet. | I hold up a bright scrap and spare my poor throat.

scene exchange4
when topic=food self.likes=blackberries
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I save berries till after the last call. | I once read a berry stain like a bit of coastline.
b : Will they hurt your voice? | Where did it take you?
a : It's the purple muzzle I'm saving my customers from. | To the basin for a wash. It had got on both cuffs.

scene exchange5
when topic=pastimes self.likes=singing
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The little tune I keep has no price in it. | I like a melody with one note I can lean against.
b : Do you sing it in public? | A long note?
a : Only if I've no cloth in my paws. | Long enough for my shoulders to come down.

scene exchange6
when topic=land self.likes=old_maps
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An old map leaves room for a whole new lane. | My map shows a stall where a stair ought to stand.
b : Where do you draw it? | Will you correct it?
a : Fold out the margin. A lane oughtn't to have to mind the border. | I put a little ladder against the stall. Both get to stay.

scene exchange7
when topic=weather self.likes=frosty_mornings
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In frost I can see how far my breath goes. | A frost line outlines my window like pale piping.
b : As far as your call? | Come loose when you touch it?
a : Barely past my nose. The rest goes on unseen. | A little oval goes clear. Just room for an eye.

scene exchange8
when topic=prices self.dislikes=haggling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'll call the marked price till my mouth's dry. | Haggling has a tune without a proper end.
b : Even to a hard bargainer? | How do you end it?
a : Especially then. A seller ought to hold one note. | Put a finger on the figure and let my mouth rest.

scene exchange9
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can hear the market's last notes from my bed. | My favourite room has one small corner with no echo.
b : Do you call back? | What fits in it?
a : I tuck my chin down and leave the work outside. | My own voice when I want a moment alone.

scene exchange10
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A missing voice takes up room in a chorus. | Some wharf cries come home in my sleep.
b : Can you sing across the gap? | Would you rather have silence?
a : I can save the space. That's enough today. | I'd rather choose which voices I kept.

scene exchange11
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can sing quietly around #self.friend#. | I'd give a friend my quiet corner at market.
b : Too shy for a loud note? | Where would you stand?
a : It's a pleasure not having to carry over a street. | Out where a loud voice earns its keep.

scene exchange12
when topic=work self.job=laborer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A wet cuff weighs down my sample cloth. | I sell the sound of a stripe first.
b : Do buyers mind? | Stripes make noise now?
a : I show the dry edge first and tell the truth about the rest. | Say 'bright red stripe' slowly. It has a snap to it.

scene exchange13
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I heard that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | A cry sounds truer from farther away.
b : Will that go into the market cry? | Does distance improve a story?
a : My voice earns pay for cloth. It can leave a rumour folded. | It hides the little tremor in the teller's breath.

scene exchange14
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Lean times take all the bounce from a bright ribbon. | I sell fewer lengths when things pinch.
b : Does the colour go? | What do people take?
a : It's still a fine red. It just hangs there longer. | Little pieces. A cuff can look new without a whole new sleeve.

scene exchange15
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I judge a turning from what happens to my voice. | A street looks shorter on the way home.
b : Does the sound split too? | Is that weariness?
a : The right wall throws it back first. | It's knowing how many cries lie between me and my door.

scene exchange16
when topic=season
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can hum my way through a winter climb. | Midwinter needs a tune with breathing space.
b : Isn't the air sharp? | What goes there?
a : I warm it behind closed teeth. | A breath through a muffler. Then the song can carry on.

scene exchange17
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like to sing against a hillside once. | I picture a day my mouth makes no money.
b : What would be on sale? | Would that suit you for a day?
a : That's the point. My tune would be out for its own pleasure. | If my belly were full and my song were mine, I would.

scene exchange18
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I rest my voice by saying colours without sound. | I keep water back for when the soft notes go.
b : Can a wolf tell which ones? | Why the soft ones?
a : Blue and brown look alike till the end. Red's unmistakable. | I can still shout when it's too late to speak gently.

story tale1 [topic=memories]
  : I used to walk past a shutter and hear another voice following mine.
  : One day I stopped to let the second caller go by. A loose slat struck the stone in exactly my time.
  b : Did you leave it loose?
  : I wedged it with a cloth end. A wolf coming off a shift deserves quiet, even if the shutter doesn't.

story tale2 [topic=pastimes self.likes=singing]
  : I sang up a stair with a piece of bright cloth between my teeth. It turned all my words to hums.
  : By the landing I had a tune I'd never meant to sing.
  b : How did you remember it?
  : I tied a knot in that cloth for each change of pitch. My tunebook fits round a wrist.

story tale3 [topic=food]
  : A berry burst on a length of waste cloth in my pocket. I meant to scrub the stain away.
  : When I shook it out, there was a purple sea with five little pale islands.
  b : Didn't it wash out?
  : I never tried. That map knows exactly where my best afternoon went.

rule @call1
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=laborer
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A clear measure of cloth and one clear price! | Colour that still looks bright in rain!

rule @call2
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Cold air gives my first note a clean edge. | First breath out. Now for the longer one.

rule @call3
when concept=bark self.dislikes=gulls
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Wings off my samples, if you please. | That call still hasn't earned a copper.

rule @call4
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say The wet hem wants another peg. | Cloth under cover till the rain moves on.
dlg resident.hub : My public voice is resting. This one works well enough.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, no need to call me over the bustle.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : The streets have stopped shouting at last.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : Say it without a sales pitch and I'll hear you.
dlg resident.job [self.job=laborer] : I cry up wares till a scrap feels like a whole bright sleeve in the mind.
dlg resident.job : I prefer ending the day knowing my pay was spoken plain.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : Here's the quiet version. #world.news#.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : I've heard #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I wouldn't give it a seller's guarantee.
dlg resident.bye : May the last voice on your walk be a kind one.

graft resident.hub
choice Can a quiet voice sell anything? -> low_note
node low_note
say Try one low note beside a shout. A wolf will turn to hear where the low one came from.
free
choice And after the first look? -> low_note_again
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node low_note_again
say Let the cloth tell the next bit. I've never met a buyer who wanted a mouthful of voice in place of a sound hem.
choice I'll leave your sample folded. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
